                <p rendition="#flush">I <hi rendition="#italic">Peace Treaty with Italy: Free
                        Territory of Trieste</hi></p>
                <p>The Deputies proceeded to consider which clauses of the Permanent Statute of the
                    Free Territory could be regarded as applicable to the Provisional Regime (see
                    docs. CFM(46) (NY) 22, 23 and 28<anchor
                        n="86" xml:id="d369-f1"/> and French Draft Instructions to the Governor for
                    the provisional period).<anchor n="87" xml:id="d369-f2"/></p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) After an exchange of views on the basis of doc.
                        CFM(46) (NY) 28, it was <hi
                        rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to report to the Ministers that the
                    following sections of this document would be applicable to the Provisional
                    Regime:</p>
                <p>Page 1, Paras. 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5:</p>
                <p>Page 2, Sections II and III, Paras. 1, 5, 8, 8 bis (1(<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>), 3(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), 10(<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a</hi>), (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)), together with the agreed texts
                    adopted at the Council’s 10th Meeting on November 28 (Withdrawal of Troops,
                    Continuance of Allied Military Government, Appointment of Governor, Appointment
                    of Provisional Council of Government (first part) and Elections to the
                    Constituent Assembly).</p>
                <pb facs="1380" n="1356" xml:id="pg1356"/>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Sub-paragraph 2 of Section III (page 2), it was
                        <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi>, would be applicable with the following
                    addition proposed by the U.S. Delegation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Without prejudice to the foregoing arrangements agreed by the Council of
                            Foreign Ministers as to the number of troops permitted in the area and
                            the conditions of their withdrawal, which shall govern the presence of
                            troops in the area during the period of the Provisional Government,
                            Article 2 of the Permanent Statute shall be applicable upon the entry
                            into force of the present Treaty.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>The U.K. Deputy drew attention in this connection to a recommendation contained
                    in para. 12 of doc. CFM(46)258, dated August
                    29, 1946,<anchor n="88" xml:id="d369-f3"/> regarding the eventual right of a
                    contingent commander to appeal to his Government against the use of his troops
                    for a particular operation.</p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Sub-paragraph 3 of Section III (page 2) was <hi
                        rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> to be applicable in conjunction with the
                    Council decision of November 28 regarding elections to the Constituent
                    Assembly.</p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>) It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> that
                    sub-paragraph 6 of Section III (page 3) was not applicable.</p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>) It was further <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >agreed</hi> that the Acting Chairman would report in detail to the
                    Ministers on the other sections of the document, the applicability of which to
                    the Provisional Regime was not agreed and would also ask the Council to give a
                    ruling as to whether the Governor should be finally responsible for executive
                    power in the provisional period.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II <hi rendition="#italic">Next Meeting</hi></p>
                <p>Monday, December 2, at 11 a.m.</p>
